  "tagline": "OLAP engine that pre-computes cubes and aggregate indexes for sub-second SQL on huge datasets.",
  "description": "Apache Kylin, open-sourced by eBay in 2014, answers SQL over billions of rows in sub-second time by pre-computing aggregates: you define a model (fact and dimension tables), Kylin builds cube or aggregate indexes with Spark, and queries are routed to the smallest matching index. Kylin 5 reworked this around flexible indexes, internal tables, a Spark-based query engine and Parquet storage. It suits stable, dimensional BI workloads with predictable queries; ad-hoc analysis and fast-changing schemas fit modern MPP engines better. Kyligence sells the commercial version.",
